Cell["\<\
Note the momenta: \[CapitalPsi][p, c, k] appears in both the bare two-point \
function and the propagator. In the former, p corresponds to the incoming \
momentum and in the former to the outgoing momentum. Thus, this expression \
describes a the propagation of a quark via P from i to k with momentum p.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977546987567437*^9, 
  3.977547142317832*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b64bd150-f840-4aa7-954a-\
3500255fb9c4"],

